### 4. Replace the entire `waitForKeyInRedis()` method

Delete its old `Probe` implementation. Replace the whole method with:

```java
public CompletableFuture<Void> waitForKeyInRedis(
    Long id,
    long committedNanos,
    ConcurrentLinkedQueue<Metric> metrics
) {
    PendingRead pending = new PendingRead(
        id,
        buildRedisKey(id),
        committedNanos
    );

    if (pendingReads.putIfAbsent(id, pending) != null) {
        return CompletableFuture.failedFuture(
            new IllegalStateException(
                "Duplicate pending ID: " + id
            )
        );
    }

    CompletableFuture<Void> collected =
        pending.result.thenAccept(metrics::add);

    long remainingNanos = Math.max(
        0L,
        TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS.toNanos(redisTimeout)
            - (System.nanoTime() - committedNanos)
    );

    try {
        ScheduledFuture<?> timeoutTask = scheduler.schedule(
            () -> timeoutPending(pending),
            remainingNanos,
            TimeUnit.NANOSECONDS
        );

        pending.result.whenComplete((metric, error) ->
            timeoutTask.cancel(false)
        );

    } catch (RuntimeException e) {
        failPending(pending, e);
    }

    return collected;
}
```

**Purpose:** instead of starting a separate polling loop, this registers the key and returns its future.

The timeout task is deliberate: **a stalled Redis request should not leave the observation future waiting indefinitely.** This strengthens the timeout behavior in the previous batch example.

### 5. Add these helper methods to `TestRunner`

Place them below `waitForKeyInRedis()`:

```java
private boolean expired(
    PendingRead pending,
    long nowNanos
) {
    return nowNanos - pending.committedNanos
        >= TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS.toNanos(redisTimeout);
}

private void timeoutPending(PendingRead pending) {
    failPending(
        pending,
        new TimeoutException(
            "Redis key not observed within "
                + redisTimeout + " ms: " + pending.key
        )
    );
}

private void failPending(
    PendingRead pending,
    Throwable error
) {
    pendingReads.remove(pending.id, pending);
    pending.result.completeExceptionally(error);
}
```

**Purpose:** centralizes removal and failure handling. Failed or timed-out observations do not become successful metrics.

### 6. Add the batch polling methods

Add both methods below the helpers:

```java
private void pollRedisBatches() {

    // Do not overlap polling rounds.
    if (!redisRoundRunning.compareAndSet(false, true)) {
        return;
    }

    List<CompletableFuture<Void>> requests =
        new ArrayList<>();

    try {
        List<PendingRead> snapshot =
            new ArrayList<>(pendingReads.values());

        for (int offset = 0;
             offset < snapshot.size();
             offset += REDIS_READ_BATCH_SIZE) {

            int end = Math.min(
                offset + REDIS_READ_BATCH_SIZE,
                snapshot.size()
            );

            List<PendingRead> batch =
                new ArrayList<>(end - offset);

            long now = System.nanoTime();

            for (int i = offset; i < end; i++) {
                PendingRead pending = snapshot.get(i);

                if (pending.result.isDone()) {
                    pendingReads.remove(pending.id, pending);

                } else if (expired(pending, now)) {
                    timeoutPending(pending);

                } else {
                    batch.add(pending);
                }
            }

            if (!batch.isEmpty()) {
                requests.add(readJsonBatch(batch));
            }
        }

    } catch (RuntimeException e) {
        pendingReads.forEach((id, pending) ->
            failPending(pending, e)
        );

    } finally {
        CompletableFuture.allOf(
            requests.toArray(new CompletableFuture<?>[0])
        ).whenComplete((ignored, error) ->
            redisRoundRunning.set(false)
        );
    }
}
```

```java
private CompletableFuture<Void> readJsonBatch(
    List<PendingRead> batch
) {
    String[] keys = batch.stream()
        .map(pending -> pending.key)
        .toArray(String[]::new);

    long submittedNanos = System.nanoTime();

    for (PendingRead pending : batch) {
        if (pending.firstCheckNanos == 0) {
            pending.firstCheckNanos = submittedNanos;
        }

        pending.checks++;
    }

    try {
        return redisClient.jsonMgetAsync(keys)
            .<Void>handle((values, error) -> {

                // Timestamp before processing the returned values.
                long observedNanos = System.nanoTime();

                try {
                    if (error != null) {
                        batch.forEach(pending ->
                            failPending(pending, error)
                        );
                        return null;
                    }

                    if (values == null
                            || values.size() != batch.size()) {
                        throw new IllegalStateException(
                            "JSON.MGET returned an unexpected response size"
                        );
                    }

                    for (int i = 0; i < batch.size(); i++) {
                        PendingRead pending = batch.get(i);

                        if (pending.result.isDone()) {
                            continue;
                        }

                        if (expired(pending, observedNanos)) {
                            timeoutPending(pending);
                            continue;
                        }

                        String json = values.get(i);

                        if (json != null) {
                            pendingReads.remove(
                                pending.id,
                                pending
                            );

                            pending.result.complete(
                                new Metric(
                                    pending.id,
                                    (observedNanos
                                        - pending.committedNanos)
                                        / 1_000_000.0,
                                    (pending.firstCheckNanos
                                        - pending.committedNanos)
                                        / 1_000_000.0,
                                    pending.checks,
                                    "INSERT"
                                )
                            );
                        }

                        // A missing key remains pending.
                    }

                } catch (RuntimeException e) {
                    batch.forEach(pending ->
                        failPending(pending, e)
                    );
                }

                return null;
            });

    } catch (RuntimeException e) {
        batch.forEach(pending -> failPending(pending, e));
        return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(null);
    }
}
```

**Purpose:**

- Take a snapshot of currently pending keys.
- Split it into groups of up to 100.
- Submit each group asynchronously.
- Complete found records immediately when their batch response arrives.
- Recheck missing records in the next round.

It **does not wait until 100 keys accumulate**. A group can contain fewer keys.

